  "scope": "GLG13-GLG15 only: actual y_v preservation of both original integral coefficient models, rational descent with original comparison/GatTies, exact NPDesc, quotient finiteness and all clauses of LatticeLengthsAtPlace. Actual compatibility/LatDefs/NuDef/NuUnserved remain premises; no existence of those producers or whole LinkG closure is inferred.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "topic": "Integral Weyl and dual-Weyl preservation",
      "result": "PASS",
      "detail": "CB2 minor-product basis bounds first-r-row degree by sum of first-r shifted weights. Homogeneous divided-power generators give the same bound for the actual Weyl submodule; scaling acts separately on each generator. Signed determinant factor and rowAct inverse orientation yield exactly z^(sum lambda_i), and two z-steps with z^2=p give the original p^ArV. Incoming edge orientation, invalid tuples and level-character equivariance match DataG."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Rational descent",
      "result": "PASS",
      "detail": "A K0-linear coefficient retraction is sufficient, with no Galois assumption. Independent comparison images give unique preimages. Invalid tuples vanish in F-span M; the rational neighbor scalar preserves all evaluations. Original GatTies plus embW_int supply the local DVR map, so flat intersections identify the actual selected P. Ordered products are retained without an unnecessary commutation premise."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Length and normalization",
      "result": "PASS",
      "detail": "Finite original lattice and p^(s+T) annihilation prove finite quotient length. Smith exponents multiply by v_O(pi_w), and original NuDef divides by e_w, giving length_O=v_O(p)*lenMN. The supported empty-served case now explicitly has J=M, tau=0, P=M cap U_F, so its local quotient is zero; NuUnserved supplies zero global length. The exceptional p=T_u branch is not incorrectly included."
    }
  ],
  "corrections_resolved": [
    "GLG14 explicitly names original GatTies for fraction-field and local coefficient-map identifications.",
    "GLG15 explicitly proves the supported empty-served branch of the first LatticeLengthsAtPlace clause."
  ],
